Vivado Simulation Flow
1. Open Xilinx Vivado and select Create Project.

2. Create a New Project
- Project Name: FIR_Noise_Reduction
- Select project location.
- Click Next.
3. Select Project Type
- Choose RTL Project.
- Select Do not specify sources at this time.
- Click Next.
4. Select FPGA Device
- Choose the required FPGA device or part.
- Click Next → Finish.
5. Add FIR Filter RTL
- Go to Flow Navigator → Add Sources.
- Select Add or Create Design Sources.
- Add fir_filter.vhd.
- Click Finish.
6. Add Testbench
- Go to Add Sources.
- Select Add or Create Simulation Sources.
- Add fir_filter_tb.vhd.
- Click Finish.
7. Set Simulation Top
- Expand Simulation Sources.
- Right-click fir_filter_tb.
- Select Set as Top.
8. Add Memory Files
- Ensure the following files are accessible from the simulator's working directory:
  - input_data.mem
  - fir_coefficients.mem
  - expected_output.mem
- Check that their paths match those specified in the testbench.
9. Configure Simulation
- Open Settings → Simulation.
- Select Vivado Simulator (XSIM).
- Confirm fir_filter_tb is the simulation top.
- Use Behavioral Simulation.
10. Run Simulation
- Go to Flow Navigator → Run Simulation → Run Behavioral Simulation.
- Wait for compilation and elaboration.
- Click Run All.
11. Add Waveform Signals
- Select the testbench or DUT instance in Scopes.
- Select the required signals in Objects.
- Right-click → Add to Wave Window.
- Click Zoom Fit.
12. Verify Output
- Check input and output waveforms.
- Compare the VHDL output with the GNU Octave reference output.
- Verify all 338 valid output samples.
- Record the actual mismatch count and simulation status.
Final flow:

Create Project → Add RTL → Add Testbench → Set Simulation Top → Add Memory Files → Configure XSIM → Run Behavioral Simulation → View Waveforms → Verify Outputs
